  "imageAlt": "Map of Babel-Ashur",
  "imageCaption": "Babel-Ashur — full island reference preserved in the archive.",
  "body": "<p>Mark of the Wild names the recorded hunting and gathering journeys undertaken from <a href=\"#skylight-refuge\">Skylight Refuge</a>. Food, components, wood, stone and metal lie beyond the camp’s concealment. Obtaining them means entering a landscape where a successful fight can still leave the company too depleted for the next one.</p><p>These journeys connect the <a href=\"#babel-survival\">larger struggle to keep a foothold</a> to its everyday work. The source dates below locate the surviving postings; they do not supply Fenumion’s calendar.</p>\n<h2 id=\"wild-camp-work\">The work that cannot be done inside the cave</h2>\n<p>In the opening January outing, Aravil lists the needs of a camp starting from bare basics: firewood, rope fibres and racks for drying hides. Aerrow scouts for useful resources; Aravil hunts and harvests; Olokun can craft; Wren and Arjahn can build. That division of work is the company’s practical account of its skills, not proof that every proposed structure is already finished.</p><p>Remaining hidden carries its own cost. Supplies run down, companions grow restless and a camp shared with survivors needs more than a place to sleep. The hunters repeatedly return to the question of what they can bring home for someone else to use.</p>\n\n<h2 id=\"wild-first-hunts\">January · victories that spend the next fight’s strength</h2>\n<p>Aerrow, Aravil and Arjahn first find buried carvings and defeat demodragons. Aravil harvests useful components. The carvings indicate earlier craftsmanship without identifying their makers or revealing a complete lost history.</p><p>With Eugene and Olokun, the company then faces an aqualisk and its demodragon companions. Olokun and Aerrow are badly hurt; Arjahn spends healing and Eugene finishes the larger creature. They continue and fight giant spiders before finally turning toward the cave. Arjahn regrets going on when so much strength has already been spent. <a href=\"#aerrow?section=aerrow-first-hunts\">Aerrow’s account</a> and <a href=\"#aravil?section=aravil-babel-hunts\">Aravil’s field work</a> show both the gains and their limits.</p>\n\n<h2 id=\"wild-retreat\">Choosing another quarry</h2>\n<p>On a later January hunt, Aravil, Aerrow and Eugene lose their advantage against an unidentified danger. They escape rather than learn its full nature through a fight. Aravil says they would need more powerful companions to face it. Its identity remains unknown.</p><p>The next encounter is a giant serpent. The party kills it and Eugene survives a serious wound, but Aravil fails the harvest. A defeated creature does not always yield the materials the hunters came for, and returning alive is a different outcome from securing everything the camp needs.</p>\n\n<h2 id=\"wild-february-loss\">February · two deaths and a later restoration</h2>\n<p>With Aravil missing, Aerrow and Arjahn leave to seek supplies. Aerrow challenges Arjahn’s desire to turn the journey into revenge, and Arjahn says he will not risk his companion for a fight. A later aqualisk encounter nevertheless overwhelms them.</p><p>The combat record establishes two deaths: Arjahn’s Revivify briefly returns Aerrow after the first, then renewed attacks kill him again. Arjahn escapes with the body. The main Babel quest later shows Elenia raising Aerrow at the Refuge. Her spell is not named in the checked passage. The <a href=\"#aerrow?section=aerrow-february-loss\">temporary return</a> and <a href=\"#aerrow?section=aerrow-return-and-warning\">later restoration</a> remain separate events.</p>\n\n<h2 id=\"wild-shared-shelter\">June and July · gathering for a shared shelter</h2>\n<p>By June the camp must also shelter rescued Babel survivors. Arjahn calls for supplies and a rear guard; Gartina leaves her stock safely behind. Scribonia offers Fabricate once the needed materials are available. Their disagreement over conversation on the trail exposes different ideas of care, without proving that the talking causes the next attack.</p><p>Gartina meets a green dragon in brass-dragon form. Saray is frightened but stays with her companions and gathers from the body after it falls. The fight shows a territorial creature defending its ground; the hunt does not by itself prove that every hostile creature serves the island’s rulers.</p><p>In July, Gartina and Arjahn discuss common metal, crafting resources and the food he once made for his family. Their work includes morale as well as material. The packet’s conditional proposal to transform and fly away is not a separate record of a completed escape.</p>\n\n<h2 id=\"wild-protection-and-coast\">September and early October · protecting, gathering and resting</h2>\n<p>Nymera joins Olokun and Scribonia while doubting whether her strength is useful beside their magic. In two spider encounters, she tries to keep the creatures from reaching her companions. Her grief accompanies active protection.</p><p>After the early October hunt, Olokun heals the group and they go to the coast where the first arrivals landed. Nymera gathers a stone she hopes Arjahn can use, then sits with her weapon nearby. Scribonia, weary after Papirak’s funeral, accepts Olokun’s company and lets a playful splash reach him. These quieter outcomes belong to the hunting history beside the defeated creatures.</p><p>The later <a href=\"#babel-survival?section=babel-path-mist\">mist expedition</a> is a separate journey. A successful hunt and a pause at the sea do not establish that the wider island has become safe.</p>\n\n<p class=\"exploration-links\">Follow the people: <a href=\"#aerrow\">Aerrow</a> · <a href=\"#aravil\">Aravil</a> · <a href=\"#arjahn\">Arjahn</a> · <a href=\"#eugene\">Eugene</a> · <a href=\"#gartina\">Gartina</a> · <a href=\"#saray\">Saray</a> · <a href=\"#nymera\">Nymera</a> · <a href=\"#olokun\">Olokun</a> · <a href=\"#scribonia\">Scribonia</a>.</p>\n\n<h2 id=\"wild-metal-and-prayer\">Seeking metal, learning how to pray</h2>\n<p><a href=\"#nymera\">Nymera</a>, <a href=\"#arjahn\">Arjahn</a> and <a href=\"#scribonia\">Scribonia</a> set out again after Scribonia’s recovery. Nymera wants useful metal; Arjahn explains that the Refuge’s planned door has consumed supplies. Their need for materials persists after the larger expedition.</p><p>On the trail, Nymera asks how to pray. Arjahn answers through his faith in Bahamut, describing prayer without requiring candles or a temple, and offers to take her to Pristinia. That offer has not yet become a visit. Their discussion of divine help and Scribonia’s possible anti-magic experiment produces no demonstrated protection against the mist.</p><p>Poisonous thorns wound Nymera before Arjahn removes a thorn and treats her. Later, two enormous spiders attack. Nymera moves to protect Scribonia, who takes brass-dragon form; Arjahn supports and heals his companions while also being bitten. Scribonia kills the first spider, and the narrator confirms lightning ends the second. The company discusses returning, with Scribonia offering Teleport. The supplied closing prose does not show the spell completed or a successful metal haul.</p>\n",
